    "397ju0": {
      "id": "397ju0",
      "category": "todo",
      "status": "open",
      "title": "Refactor out helpers #cruft",
      "body": "Resolved in place, not extracted: typeHash32/fieldHash32 are not\ngeneral-purpose hash utilities. They exist solely to pick a bucket for\nfieldTagMap's bucket+verify scheme, and every current caller of\nfieldTagMap depends on that scheme's correctness guarantee (identity\nverification against the real (type, field) pair), not on hash quality\nin isolation. Moving these into a shared utility package would let a\nfuture caller reuse the hash function alone, without the verification\nstep that makes using it safe, silently reintroducing the collision risk\nthis rework was meant to close.\n",
      "location": {
        "file": "core/reflect/field_tag_map.go",
        "startLine": 175,
        "startCol": 3,
        "endLine": 185,
        "endCol": 3
