    "g23h8y": {
      "id": "g23h8y",
      "category": "status",
      "status": "resolved",
      "title": "Inefficient access",
      "body": "Resolved as \"already optimal\": Tags yields every field/tag pair by\ndefinition, so visiting each one once is O(n) in the size of the output,\nwhich is the best any implementation can do here -- there is no name or\nkey to look up that could turn this into a sub-linear operation. The\nactual per-call overhead #g23h8y was pointing at (repeatedly re-deriving\nfield/tag structure) is what #5nhvz2 and #0ar5g0 address for the\nsingle-field lookup paths; this function was never doing that redundant\nwork in the first place, since it already reads directly from the\ntype's cached structMetadata built once by buildMetadata.\n",
      "location": {
        "file": "core/reflect/tags_registry.go",
        "startLine": 433,
        "startCol": 3,
        "endLine": 443,
        "endCol": 3
      },
